# Work plan

Same discipline as account manager: a written spec, then a written plan, then one slice. Do not wander into the next idea mid-task.

- A new capability, a behavior change, or a visual pass starts in `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` (goal, decisions, non-goals) and `docs/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` (ordered tasks with the files each one touches).
- Build only the current task. A follow-up the user names while you are in a slice goes into the spec as a later task, not into the code you are writing.
- Finish a slice by verifying it (typecheck, and the browser for UI) before opening the next one.
- A one-line copy or label fix does not need a spec. Anything that changes money, status, navigation, or layout does.
- Do not restyle a screen with one-off classes. Visual work follows `DESIGN.md` and `.cursor/rules/smilesim-ui.mdc`.
